{"question_id":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-main-scale-reference-line-co-jee-main-physics-lzve1z4yf6whnob7","qKey":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-main-scale-reference-line-co-jee-main-physics-lzve1z4yf6whnob7","permalink":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-main-scale-reference-line-co-jee-main-physics-lzve1z4yf6whnob7","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift","year":2026,"subject":"physics","chapter":"units-and-measurements","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>In a screw gauge the zero of main scale reference line coincides with the fifth division of the circular scale when two studs are in contact. There are 100 divisions in circular scale and pitch of screw gauge is 0.1 mm. When diameter of a sphere is measured, the reading of main scale is 5 mm and 50<sup>th</sup> division of circular scale coincides with the reference line of main scale. The diameter of sphere is ______ mm.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>5.045</p>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>5.055</p>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>5.450</p>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>5.550</p>"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>The least count is the smallest distance the screw moves when the circular scale is rotated by one division. It is defined as:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.158ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"59.095ex\" height=\"3.447ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1011.8 26119.9 1523.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0Least Count\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8077.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(9133.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(7008.2,481.4) scale(0.707)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0Pitch\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(220,-370.3) scale(0.707)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0Number of divisions on circular scale\u00a0</text></g><rect width=\"16746.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>The pitch is linear distance moved in one complete rotation. The pitch of screw gauge is given as 0.1 mm and there are 100 divisions:</p>\n<p>So, the least count is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.816ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"26.027ex\" height=\"3.105ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1011.8 11504.1 1372.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(625,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1624.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2680.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,481.4) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500